      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Blood pressure is 118 over 76. Pulse 66. Temperature 36.6 degrees. Respiratory rate 14. Oxygen saturation 99 percent, and your weight is 71 kilograms.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:35",
      "end_timestamp": "02:47",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[0]",
        "vital_signs[1]",
        "vital_signs[2]",
        "vital_signs[3]",
        "vital_signs[4]",
        "vital_signs[5]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Under the lamp the patches on both hands and the elbows are chalk-white with very sharp edges. That's a typical appearance.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:57",
      "end_timestamp": "04:09",
      "supports": [
        "physical_examination[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "This looks like vitiligo. It's a fairly common condition, and it happens when the immune system mistakenly targets the pigment cells.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:46",
      "end_timestamp": "04:57",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Could you print the leaflet on sun protection for him? Thanks. Now, one more piece of my reasoning. Vitiligo is sometimes seen together with thyroid problems, so I'd like to order a thyroid blood test.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:42",
      "end_timestamp": "05:59",
      "supports": [
        "procedures_and_investigations[0]",
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "The patches are very exposed to sun, because those cells don't protect the skin anymore. So please use a high factor sunscreen on your hands and elbows, especially in summer, or you'll burn.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:17",
      "end_timestamp": "06:37",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I'd like to see you again in six weeks, so we can go over the results and decide on a plan together.",
